November 20, 1992 Friday 11:26:21 pmUUCP Package Changes by Mike Haaland (mike@htsmm1.las-vegas.nv.us)I think Bob Larson has done a 'bang-up' job in giving us somethingto build on with his post of 'BLARSUUCP'.  Unforch, you have to usehis library to compile it.  This wouldn't be a problem, except youhave to have source for the lib in order to get some of the 'site'dependancies and name of the password file to match what most folksalready have set up.  I've attempted to duplicate or delete the needfor those particular functions.  And the result is; an extremelyconfigurable UUCP package that we can distribute as binaries.The system is much more complete now, but we still need a good portof ELM and SMail.  I've been using the TOPs Smail and OXM, they workbut have some compatibility problems if you want to use alternatepassword files or the pw_gecos field for fullnames.  Another problemwith Smail is that it won't put the entire 'host.domain' in the Fromline on out-going messages.  This messes up some Internet hosts tryingto return errors to the correct person.If you plan on doing Netnews I will be distributing a modified versionof Cnews and RN at a later date.These are the programs that the package now consists of:    uucico  - Major changes, see below for details    uux    uuxqt   - NEW one    uucp    -     (Now expands tilde if used for the Host system)    uupoll  - Changed the name of Pollfile to C.systemPOLL (for uuclean)    uuname  - NEW (list UUCP neighbors)    uuclean - NEW (Rotate logfiles and notify/return old que'd mail)    uulog   - NEW (Display logfiles)    uustat  - NEW (Show/delete/rejuvinate incoming/outgoing UUCP jobs)    mail    - NEW (Command line mailer - May be used interactivly)                  (reads from stdin forks smail - translates EOL if needed)    lmail   - NEW (put mail in the users mailbox)                  (Forked by smail to deliver local mail)    rmail   - NEW (Forks smail to route incoming mail)                  This is needed to translate LF's to CR's so the TOPs                  smail doesn't choke.All the utilities now check the config file to get system setups.  Andevery reference to /H0 has been changed to /DD.  This allows using anydevice desired.References to MTSmon below are to Carl Kreider's MTSmon.Following are some of the changes that have been made to the package: uucico - MSH    o Added HDB style Dialers, Devices and Systems files.      Dialers file can contain login, reset and error strings.      This allows the use of many different init/reset strings      for the same of different devices and even for different      baud rates.    o Added expansion of '~' tilde to emulate UNIX expansion.      IE: ~uucp and ~/ both translate to the pubdir, ~username      expands to the HOME directory of the user.    o Moved the default LIBDIR to /DD/USR/LIB/UUCP, but only the      a Config file needs to be there.  (Much like Taylor UUCP)    o Added a Config file for redefining all paths, configuration      files, login name uucp user, machine name, even the name      of the password file can be redefined, etc.  (Like Taylor UUCP)    o Added pwent.c and pwd.h to handle all the password functions.    o uucico can now turn mtsmon on/off as needed to free a port up.    o Changed uucico to check for work que'd after it is done receiving,      before it just hung up.    o Fixed setline() so it doesn't mess with the High-bit in the parity      byte.  Some systems use this bit to indicate hardware handshaking.    o Changed the format of the logfile to be easier to read with uulog.    o Changed the expect() to allow \s to be interpreted as a space.    o Also changed the backslash characters to be more like UNIX UUCP.      \t is tab, \T sends the phone number, \nnn will send an octal code.      these backslash codes ARE case sensitive as with other UUCPs.    o Changed the way the port is handled, if the port is busy, check to      see if mtsmon is running, if so, turn off mtsmon and retry the port.    o Added code to check if uuxqt is already running before executing it.December 9, 1992 Wednesday 3:19:43 pm  pwent.c - MSH    o Changed pwent.c routines to actually store gid/uid in a binary      format instead of ASCII format.  This makes it easier to use      the fields in the PWENT struct and is more like UNIX.    o Added pw_giduid - this value is compatible with getuid()January 17, 1993 Sunday 1:07:58 am  dcpgpkt.c - MSH    o Added negotiation for sliding window size and varable packet      handling.    o Added file restriction access by site. (Permissions file)  uuxqt.c    o Added commands restriction by site. (Permissions file)  This      allows a large selection of commands available in Commands      file while restricting any sites desired to a limited list of      actual commands it may request to execute.